  "description": "PUTROM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H64 Cl2 Dy6 O30 4+,4(Cl1 1-),16(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.513-3.726 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.54-109.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ3-OH)4L4L′2(H2O)9Cl]Cl5·15H2O (L = o-vanillinate; L′ = 2-hydroxymethyl-6-methoxyphenolate); C48H96Cl6O46Dy6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 9 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 9 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
